   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kontext-edit.json\n\nRelight (Kontext, superseded)\n\nE13 - instruction-based relight with Flux.1 Kontext dev fp8. Kontext works at ~1 MP (FluxKontextImageScale 2048x1024 -> 1456x720), so the 4x-UltraSharp + ImageScale tail RESTORES the original resolution - that pairing is the whole point. guidance 2.5, cfg 1.0 (Flux is distilled: cfg is unused), 20 steps, ~69 s. Compare against ColorMatch (3 s): colour transfer reproduces the global palette but CANNOT add the sun / directional highlights / contact shadow. Colour statistics are not illumination. ALSO: LoadImage reads only from input/ - stage upstream images into input/2d/_work/, never input/2d/ (anything there gets swept into assets/ by publish_assets.sh).\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S5** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E13 -> see U2** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  }
